{
  "id": "c1-e14-ethics-of-science-and-ai",
  "level": "C1",
  "version": 1,
  "topic": "Ethics of science and AI",
  "parts": [
    {
      "index": 1,
      "title": "Interview",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "p1-intro",
          "kind": "narration",
          "text": "Good evening. First of all, we'd like to know a little about you.",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e14-ethics-of-science-and-ai/p1-intro.mp3",
          "audioMs": 4400
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-q1",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "A",
          "text": "Candidate A, how interested are you in science and new discoveries?",
          "durationSec": 25,
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e14-ethics-of-science-and-ai/p1-q1.mp3",
          "audioMs": 5000
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-q2",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "B",
          "text": "Candidate B, what recent technological development has impressed you most?",
          "durationSec": 25,
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e14-ethics-of-science-and-ai/p1-q2.mp3",
          "audioMs": 5500
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-q3",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "A",
          "text": "Candidate A, do you trust what scientists tell us?",
          "durationSec": 30,
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e14-ethics-of-science-and-ai/p1-q3.mp3",
          "audioMs": 3700
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-q4",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "B",
          "text": "Candidate B, how do you think science will change daily life in the future?",
          "durationSec": 30,
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e14-ethics-of-science-and-ai/p1-q4.mp3",
          "audioMs": 5300
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "title": "Long turn",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "p2-intro",
          "kind": "narration",
          "text": "In this part of the test, I'm going to give each of you three pictures. I'd like you to talk about two of them on your own for about a minute, and also to answer a question briefly about your partner's pictures.",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e14-ethics-of-science-and-ai/p2-intro.mp3",
          "audioMs": 13200
        },
        {
          "id": "p2-a",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "A",
          "durationSec": 60,
          "assets": [
            "c1-e14-a1",
            "c1-e14-a2",
            "c1-e14-a3"
          ],
          "text": "Candidate A, your pictures show people working with advanced technology. Choose two of the pictures and say what benefits this technology might bring, and what concerns people might have.",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e14-ethics-of-science-and-ai/p2-a.mp3",
          "audioMs": 12400
        },
        {
          "id": "p2-a-follow",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "B",
          "durationSec": 30,
          "text": "Candidate B, which of these developments do you find the most exciting?",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e14-ethics-of-science-and-ai/p2-a-follow.mp3",
          "audioMs": 5100
        },
        {
          "id": "p2-b",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "B",
          "durationSec": 60,
          "assets": [
            "c1-e14-b1",
            "c1-e14-b2",
            "c1-e14-b3"
          ],
          "text": "Candidate B, your pictures show technology making decisions or doing tasks. Choose two of the pictures and say how people might feel about relying on this technology, and what could go wrong.",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e14-ethics-of-science-and-ai/p2-b.mp3",
          "audioMs": 13300
        },
        {
          "id": "p2-b-follow",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "A",
          "durationSec": 30,
          "text": "Candidate A, would you feel safe using this technology?",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e14-ethics-of-science-and-ai/p2-b-follow.mp3",
          "audioMs": 4200
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "title": "Collaborative task",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "p3-intro",
          "kind": "narration",
          "text": "Now I'd like you to talk about something together for about two minutes. Here are some questions raised by new scientific and technological developments, and a question for you to discuss.",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e14-ethics-of-science-and-ai/p3-intro.mp3",
          "audioMs": 12300
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-discuss",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "both",
          "durationSec": 120,
          "diagram": "c1-e14-ethics-of-science-and-ai",
          "text": "Talk to each other about this question: How important is it to consider these issues before using new technology?",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e14-ethics-of-science-and-ai/p3-discuss.mp3",
          "audioMs": 8200
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-decide",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "both",
          "durationSec": 60,
          "diagram": "c1-e14-ethics-of-science-and-ai",
          "text": "Now you have about a minute to decide together. Which issue is the most urgent to resolve?",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e14-ethics-of-science-and-ai/p3-decide.mp3",
          "audioMs": 6500
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "title": "Discussion",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "p4-intro",
          "kind": "narration",
          "text": "Now I'd like to ask you some more questions about ethics in science and artificial intelligence.",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e14-ethics-of-science-and-ai/p4-intro.mp3",
          "audioMs": 6900
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-q1",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "both",
          "durationSec": 50,
          "text": "Should there be limits on what scientists are allowed to research?",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e14-ethics-of-science-and-ai/p4-q1.mp3",
          "audioMs": 4400
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-q2",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "A",
          "durationSec": 45,
          "text": "Candidate A, to what extent can we rely on machines to make important decisions?",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e14-ethics-of-science-and-ai/p4-q2.mp3",
          "audioMs": 6200
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-q3",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "B",
          "durationSec": 45,
          "text": "Candidate B, who should decide how artificial intelligence is regulated, governments or companies?",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e14-ethics-of-science-and-ai/p4-q3.mp3",
          "audioMs": 7400
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-q4",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "both",
          "durationSec": 50,
          "text": "Is there a danger that technology could increase inequality between rich and poor?",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e14-ethics-of-science-and-ai/p4-q4.mp3",
          "audioMs": 6100
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-q5",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "A",
          "durationSec": 45,
          "text": "Candidate A, do you think the benefits of genetic research outweigh the risks?",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e14-ethics-of-science-and-ai/p4-q5.mp3",
          "audioMs": 5700
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-q6",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "B",
          "durationSec": 45,
          "text": "Candidate B, how can ordinary people make sure they are informed about new developments?",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e14-ethics-of-science-and-ai/p4-q6.mp3",
          "audioMs": 6300
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
